  "caption": "Quinn reached for the top shelf and the shoulder said no — for the third time this year. Cuff exercises were done, posture alarms were buzzing, and the pain kept coming back.\n\nRecurring shoulder pain often involves the shoulder blade not moving well, which rotator cuff work alone can miss. Active muscle training tends to change it more than posture reminders.\n\nWhat can help: having the movement pattern assessed, starting with activation exercises, progressing in phases to loaded overhead work, and freeing up a stiff upper back.\n\nGet it checked after a fall or injury, or if you notice sudden weakness, a deformity, numbness spreading down the arm, or symptoms lasting beyond 6–8 weeks. Chest tightness with shoulder pain needs urgent medical help.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
